All 15 tests now pass. Here's what I fixed in `src/`:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission`: changed from literal membership (`required in user_roles`) to case-insensitive comparison (`any(role.lower() == required.lower() ...)`).
- `is_admin_or_owner`: changed `and` to `or` so that being either an admin *or* the owner grants access.

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__`: replaced the mutable default argument `{}` with `None` + `self._stock = dict(initial) if initial is not None else {}`, preventing shared state across instances.
- `add`: changed from overwriting (`= qty`) to accumulating (`+= qty`) stock.
- `reserve`: changed the boundary check from `>=` to `>` so that reserving exactly the available amount is allowed.
- `release`: added a guard to raise `ValueError` when releasing more than the currently reserved quantity.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify`: lowercased alphanumeric characters and replaced the single `replace("--", "-")` with a `while "--" in collapsed` loop to collapse arbitrary runs of repeated separators.
- `truncate`: subtracted `len(suffix)` from the kept prefix length so the total output respects `max_len`.
